        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>Element Name</td><td>Type</td><td>Semantics</td></tr><tr><td>Header</td><td>complexType: MessageHeaderType Refer to 8.3.3</td><td>Contains general information, used for all messages.</td></tr><tr><td>ResponseCode</td><td>simpleType: responseCodeType enumeration refer to Annex A for the type definition</td><td>ResponseCode indicating the acknowledgment status of any of the V2G messages received by the SECC.</td></tr><tr><td>ServiceRenegotiationSupported</td><td>simpleType: xs:boolean</td><td>If set to &quot;True&quot; the SECC is capable of ServiceRenegotiation as specified in this document. If set to &quot;FALSE&quot; the SECC is not capable of ServiceRenegotiation. The value of this parameter is valid throughout the service session.</td></tr><tr><td>EnergyTransferServiceList</td><td>complexType: ServiceListType refer to 8.3.5.3.2</td><td>Available energy transfer and BPT services supported by the EVSE.</td></tr><tr><td>VASList</td><td>complexType: ServiceListType refer to 8.3.5.3.2</td><td>Optional: A list containing information on all other services than energy transfer services offered by the EVSE. The returned service list is a filtered list based on the SupportedServiceIDs indicated in the ServiceDiscoveryReq message. The number of service elements is limited to eight.</td></tr></table>",
